Buyer RPC security matrix for AUTH-01, closing the evidence gap from the
prior certification commit (93ca72a), which had only 9/36 RPCs body-read
and the rest grant-verified only.

All 36 entries in buyer-deployment-rpc-allowlist.ts / verify-contract-
boundary.mjs are now individually classified (PUBLIC SAFE / PRE-LOGIN
PUBLIC INTAKE / AUTHENTICATED BUYER / BUYER + STAFF / INTERNAL ONLY) with
direct evidence: exact migration file, company-derivation mechanism,
cross-company protection, and frozen/inactive handling for each.

Two real Core defects were found during this body audit and fixed on a
separate Core branch (auth01-rpc-staff-exclusion-fix, not this repo):

- customer_order_status_v1 / customer_order_items_v1 /
  customer_support_tickets_v1 used an inline eligibility gate with no role
  filter and no staff exclusion, unlike the canonical
  customer_buyer_eligible_company_id() helper introduced later for exactly
  this family. Core commit 8a81780 fixes all three to call the canonical
  helper, plus a pgTAP regression (not run -- no live Postgres in this
  sandbox).
- get_sales_order_pi_final_payment_request_v1 and its three governing RLS
