Subject: [PATCH 07/11] fix(orders): checkout-success banner persists
 indefinitely across tab revisits

Bug-search pass, continued (broken navigation / stale state category).

Repro: complete a checkout -> navigation.replace('MainTabs', { screen:
'Orders', params: { checkoutSuccess: {...} } }) lands the buyer on Orders
with that param set. OrdersScreen reads route.params?.checkoutSuccess and
renders the success banner, but nothing ever clears it. MainTabNavigator
sets no unmountOnBlur on the Orders tab (correctly -- that would also
discard the rest of the screen's state), so per standard React Navigation
bottom-tabs behavior, the route's params persist across tab switches. The
banner ('Sales Order created', order number, value, advance) reappears
every single time the buyer revisits the Orders tab afterwards -- for an
order that may be long since dispatched, days or weeks later -- not just
once as intended.

Fix: clear checkoutSuccess via navigation.setParams({ checkoutSuccess:
undefined }) in an effect keyed on its presence, which runs after the
render that displays it (not before), so it still shows exactly once on
arrival and never again on a later tab revisit.

No test added: this is React Navigation param/tab-lifecycle behavior,
which (like the two fixes in 69b7801) this repo's plain node:test
convention doesn't cover without a component-rendering framework (no RNTL
here). Verified manually via code trace of MainTabNavigator's Tab.Screen
config (no unmountOnBlur) and OrdersScreen's param read.

Verified: npm run quality passes end to end -- 164/164 tests (unchanged),
typecheck clean, lint clean, rc-navigation-audit and rc-forensic-scan both
pass, boundary/cert:bindings/census:p106/expo-config all clean.

No production mutation of any kind.
