Bugsweep-01 Phase B: regression coverage and verification for the two
newest fixes (111e607), per the explicit checklist.

1. AppState foreground eligibility revalidation

   Extracted the pure trigger decisions into
   buyer-session-refresh-triggers.ts: shouldRefreshOnAuthEvent (skips only
   TOKEN_REFRESHED) and shouldRefreshOnAppState (refreshes only on
   transition to 'active'). Both are now direct-tested (5 assertions) --
   the previous version of this logic was inline and, like
   claimApprovedB2bIdentity()/resolveBuyerSession(), untestable without
   pulling react-native into node:test.

   While reviewing against the checklist, found and fixed a real gap:
   refresh() had no in-flight deduplication. An auth event and an AppState
   foreground transition can fire within the same tick (e.g. the app is
   resumed right as a background token refresh completes), and each would
   have started its own resolveBuyerSession() call -- a genuine 'refresh
   storm' / 'parallel eligibility refresh' risk, exactly what the checklist
   asked to verify against. Fixed with a shared in-flight promise
   (inFlightRefreshRef): concurrent callers now await the same request
   instead of each firing their own. The existing requestId staleness guard
   already protected correctness (a stale response was always discarded),
   so this closes a real efficiency/redundant-request gap, not a
   correctness bug.

   Verified by code trace, not by a fresh defect: does not recurse through
   auth events (the listener only calls refresh(), which no longer
   re-triggers onAuthStateChange itself), handles offline foreground
   gracefully (resolveBuyerSession() already fails closed to
   backend_failure rather than hanging), and an active valid buyer's
   snapshot is simply re-confirmed as approved_buyer, not disturbed.

2. Concurrent-checkout losing-client UX

   Extracted classifyCheckoutSubmitError() (checkout-submit-error.ts):
   classification is by ParsedRpcError.code, not message string-matching,
   confirmed directly by a test that also proves DRAFT_NOT_READY,
   PRODUCT_UNAVAILABLE, AUTH_REQUIRED, and UNKNOWN are never misclassified
   as concurrent promotion. CheckoutScreen.tsx now calls this instead of
   inlining the branch. View Orders navigates to the real MainTabs/Orders
   route (unchanged, already valid). draftAlreadySubmittedElsewhere is
   reset to false at the start of both loadCheckout() and submitOrder(), so
   a reload/retry clears the stale flag before a new attempt.

