From d671da8a4971a8b0cb8cd3746af75fac74be4024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AUTH-01 Native Convergence <auth01-agent@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:02:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(support,genie): call v2 ticket RPC, feature-gate
 ai-order-parse

Corrects two rollout issues per governed-release review.

1. Switch ticket submission from v1 to v2

   Core's rollout architecture was corrected (backward-compatible v1/v2,
   not a breaking v1 signature change -- see branch
   support-ticket-idempotency-v2). This app now calls
   submit_customer_support_ticket_v2 instead of v1: database.types.ts,
   customerGateway.ts, buyer-deployment-rpc-allowlist.ts, and
   verify-contract-boundary.mjs all updated together (boundary verify
   passes). support-ticket-idempotency.ts/.test.ts comments updated to
   reference the current v2 migration instead of the superseded
   single-version approach.

2. Feature-gate Oasis Genie order parsing (all four modes)

   Production inspection established that tcxvcatsqqertcnycuop (the exact
   Supabase project this app's own supabaseUrl points at) has no deployed
   Edge Function named ai-order-parse, and it exists in source in none of
   the three governed repositories. Every Genie parse mode -- text, audio,
   image, document -- funnels through the same invokeGenieOrderParse()
   call to that one slug. Before this fix, only 'audio' had an honest
   'not yet available' message; 'text' and 'image'/'document' looked live
   (enabled button, no warning) but would fail at runtime the moment a
   buyer actually tried them.

   Classified as deferred, not launch-enabled, for this pass: designing,
   sourcing, and certifying a real ai-order-parse function (authenticated
   identity, server-derived company authority, MIME/size validation,
   defined retention, verify_jwt) is new feature work far beyond a
   bugsweep, and the instructions are explicit that a fabricated fallback
   parser is not an acceptable alternative.

   - Add genie-parse-availability.ts: a single zero-dependency
     GENIE_PARSE_ENABLED = false constant (no supabase, no react-native
     import), so it's directly unit-testable and importable by the actual
     network chokepoint, not just the UI screen.
   - genie-order-parse.ts's invokeGenieOrderParse() now checks this flag
     and throws before ever calling supabase.functions.invoke(
     'ai-order-parse', ...) -- enforcement at the chokepoint every mode
     shares, not only at the screen level. A future call site that
     imports invokeGenieOrderParse directly, bypassing AiOrderScreen,
     is protected too.
   - AiOrderScreen.tsx: all four mode tabs now show an explicit
     unavailable message (previously only audio did); the Parse/Choose
     button is disabled for every mode; the text-entry TextInput itself is
     replaced by the unavailable message rather than accepting input that
     could never be parsed.

Add genie-parse-availability.test.ts: proves the gate is off, with the
full evidence trail in the assertion description -- the required
regression proving the deferred feature cannot call production.

Verified: npm run quality passes end to end -- 173/173 tests (1 new),
typecheck clean, lint clean, boundary/rc-scan/rc-navigation/cert:bindings/
census:p106/expo-config all pass. Diff reviewed: contained to the two
intended changes, no secrets, no service-role usage, no RLS touched.

No production mutation of any kind.
